1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:01,759
What if a kingdom's
most beloved

2
00:00:01,779 --> 00:00:04,578
festival began as a
punishment?

3
00:00:04,598 --> 00:00:06,021
On Bellnight,
Dunmere camps

4
00:00:06,041 --> 00:00:07,709
outside its own
walls:

5
00:00:07,729 --> 00:00:09,121
bells,
bonfires,

6
00:00:09,141 --> 00:00:11,650
a cheer when the
gates open at dawn.

7
00:00:11,670 --> 00:00:12,991
Three hundred years
ago,

8
00:00:13,011 --> 00:00:14,729
a king locked them
out for one winter

9
00:00:14,749 --> 00:00:15,741
night.

10
00:00:15,991 --> 00:00:17,127
Bells,
to find each other

11
00:00:17,147 --> 00:00:18,090
in the snow.

12
00:00:18,110 --> 00:00:20,386
Fires,
to live till morning.

13
00:00:20,406 --> 00:00:21,379
The cheer at dawn?

14
00:00:21,399 --> 00:00:22,766
A head count.

15
00:00:22,966 --> 00:00:24,302
The custom survived.

16
00:00:24,322 --> 00:00:26,227
The reason was
forgotten.

17
00:00:26,463 --> 00:00:28,405
Invent a tradition
and tell us how it

18
00:00:28,425 --> 00:00:29,568
began.
